    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Invoice Automation – WhatsApp Delivery\nOriginal build tested end-to-end: 2026-07-09 | Revised: 2026-10-07 (retest pending)\nAuthor: Taha Tahir\n\nEvery 2 hours: fetches posted invoices that have no 'sent' row in the audit table, checks the customer has a WhatsApp number, signs a 1-hour link to the PDF webhook, sends via Twilio, and logs every outcome (sent / skipped / failed) to Postgres. Every branch loops back, so one bad invoice never stops the run.\n\nDepends on: **Serve Invoice PDFs** being Active, and the same PDF_LINK_SECRET in the n8n environment (it signs links here and verifies them there).",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 1400
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -304,
        -624
      ],
      "id": "f020a81e-31e3-45c5-8ea0-fd955457d6d7",
      "name": "Sticky Note"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Why this filter exists\nOdoo returns `false` (not null/empty string) for blank fields.\nNaive \"is not empty\" checks let blank numbers through silently.\nExplicit check: `field && field !== false ? field : ''`\nFull writeup: DEBUGGING_LOG.md, bug #6",
        "height": 272,
        "width": 448,
        "color": "#FFCE47"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1400,
        -576
      ],
      "id": "38e3f95f-de38-4e94-96b5-b28a5f40199b",
      "name": "Sticky Note1"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### For future reference\n- delivery_status now writes 'sent', 'skipped_no_phone', 'skipped_invalid_phone' or 'failed'\n- 'sent' means Twilio accepted the message (status queued), not that WhatsApp delivered it. A Twilio status callback would close that gap.\n- No automatic retry: skipped and failed invoices are simply picked up again on the next scheduled run (only 'sent' invoices are excluded).",
        "height": 304,
        "width": 420,
        "color": "#90BBEA"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        3216,
        -336
      ],
      "id": "317ad046-2d3f-4ba1-860c-aafde2842e09",
      "name": "Sticky Note2"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "feb3839d-aa30-468b-98e4-b2c1d02dbc79",
              "name": "phone_e164",
              "value": "={{ (() => {\n  const raw = String($json.result[0].mobile || '').trim();\n  const cc = String($env.DEFAULT_COUNTRY_CODE || '').replace(/\\D/g, '');\n  const d = raw.replace(/[^\\d+]/g, '');\n  let out;\n  if (d.startsWith('+')) out = '+' + d.slice(1).replace(/\\D/g, '');\n  else if (d.startsWith('00')) out = '+' + d.slice(2);\n  else if (d.startsWith('0') && cc) out = '+' + cc + d.slice(1);\n  else out = d ? '+' + d : '';\n  return /^\\+[1-9]\\d{7,14}$/.test(out) ? out : '';\n})() }}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "includeOtherFields": true,
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        1696,
        -144
      ],
      "id": "dd621564-4e1b-457b-bc44-563f3cc8529e",
      "name": "Normalize Phone"
    },
